{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Localization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How the default placeholders’ built-in text is localized, how to add a language, and how to show different text instead without touching ScreenStates itself."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The default Empty\/Loading\/Error placeholders’ text — “Nothing Here,” “Loading,” “Retry,” “Something Went Wrong,” “Connection Issue” — comes from a String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":", resolved from ScreenStates’ own bundle ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bundle.module"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than your app’s. That’s deliberate: a custom title your app passes in (see below) is never run back through localization, and a language you add to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"your own"}]},{"type":"text","text":" app’s catalog has no effect on these five strings — they only ever resolve against ScreenStates’ bundle. English, Spanish, French, and Russian are built in today."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Adding a language to ScreenStates","anchor":"Adding-a-language-to-ScreenStates"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is a change to the package itself, not something a consuming app can do on its own — it needs a PR. Open "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Resources\/Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" and add a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"localizations"},{"type":"text","text":" entry for the new language code under each of the five string keys:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["\"Retry\" : {","  \"comment\" : \"Title of the button that retries loading after an error.\",","  \"localizations\" : {","    \"en\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Retry\" } },","    \"de\" : { \"stringUnit\" : { \"state\" : \"translated\", \"value\" : \"Wiederholen\" } }","  }","}"],"syntax":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every one of the five keys needs an entry for every language — a string present in English but missing a translation elsewhere fails CI (see below). "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStatesStrings.swift"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s doc comments list all five keys and their English text if you’re starting from scratch."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Overriding text per-app","anchor":"Overriding-text-per-app","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You don’t need a new language, or a PR, to show different text than the built-in default — two options, depending on how much you want to replace:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"title"},{"type":"text","text":" directly, bypassing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Localizable.xcstrings"},{"type":"text","text":" entirely for that one string. Pass your own localized string (from your own app’s String Catalog, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NSLocalizedString"},{"type":"text","text":", whatever) instead of the default:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["ScreenStateDefaultEmptyView(title: String(localized: \"No Results\"))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ScreenStateDefaultErrorView"},{"type":"text","text":" has no equivalent for its title or Retry button text today — only the error’s own message is customizable, via "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"For anything else — the Error placeholder’s title, the Retry button’s text, or any text at all in a shape the built-in views don’t expose a parameter for — pass a fully custom placeholder instead of the default one, via ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference"},{"text":"’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"loading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" builder closures (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","type":"reference"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","type":"reference"},{"text":") or ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateViewController","type":"reference"},{"text":"‘s equivalent. A custom placeholder can still reuse ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement","type":"reference"},{"text":" so VoiceOver announces transitions with the same wording your custom text uses, instead of the default’s.","type":"text"}]}]}]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/screenstates\/localization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Related-Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithUIKit","doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility"],"title":"Related Documentation"}],"metadata":{"title":"Localization","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article"},"references":{"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/Accessibility":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/Accessibility","abstract":[{"text":"Everything the default placeholders — and your own custom ones — get for free: VoiceOver, Reduce Motion, Increase Contrast, Dynamic Type, and stable identifiers for XCUITest.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/accessibility","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Accessibility"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/gettingstartedwithswiftui","abstract":[{"text":"Drive a SwiftUI screen’s four states with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"title":"Getting Started with SwiftUI","role":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/GettingStartedWithSwiftUI"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateContainerView":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateContainerView","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UIView"},{"type":"text","text":" that swaps its content for the right placeholder based on a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", mirroring "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateView","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" from the SwiftUI side."}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatecontainerview","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateContainerView"}],"type":"topic","title":"ScreenStateContainerView"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScreenState","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The four canonical states of a screen: nothing to show yet, in flight,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"showing data, or failed."}],"title":"ScreenState","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenStateDisplayableError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstatedisplayableerror","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScreenStateDisplayableError"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Lets an error type supply its own user-facing message, distinct from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localizedDescription","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — which is often a debugging string (or, for a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"plain ","type":"text"},{"code":"Error","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" with no ","type":"text"},{"code":"CustomStringConvertible","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":"LocalizedError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conformance, just the type name) rather than something to put in front","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of the person using the app.","type":"text"}],"title":"ScreenStateDisplayableError","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateDisplayableError"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/ScreenState/accessibilityAnnouncement":{"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/screenstates\/screenstate\/accessibilityannouncement","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"accessibilityAnnouncement"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The same text the default placeholders announce to VoiceOver for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this case, reusable by a fully custom placeholder that wants to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announce transitions with the same wording instead of inventing its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own. "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for "},{"code":".data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", since at that point a custom placeholder’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"own content is what VoiceOver should read, not a transition"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"announcement."}],"title":"accessibilityAnnouncement","role":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenState\/accessibilityAnnouncement"},"doc://screenstates.ScreenStates/documentation/ScreenStates/GettingStar